# memory_gap_table_rewrite: The guest rewrites a leaf after the host has used it. Buffer A's object keeps the pages it was made over in every setup (objects are cached by reference): a fill through A after VA 8's leaf moves from page P1 to P2 lands in P1. A new buffer B over VA 8 differs by setup: in the blocks setup VA 8 is still mapped in the host task (the range tracker says so), so B's fill lands in P1 too; in the map and isolate setups a buffer is a new mapping of the table as it is now, and it lands in P2. After an unmap of VA 8 (34) a third buffer C lands in P2 in every setup: the blocks setup maps the page again. Command buffers are read through the table at every exec: after VA 4's leaf moves to page P3, which holds another command buffer, the same range runs P3's.
